### TM Forum Open API v5 — `assets/tmforum/`

**Two of the three are redistributed, under Apache-2.0.** `TMF620-Product_Catalog_Management-v5.0.0.oas.yaml`
and `TMF622-ProductOrdering-v5.0.0.oas.yaml`, taken from the `tmforum-apis` GitHub organisation at recorded
upstream commits. `assets/tmforum/LICENSE` is the Apache-2.0 text as published there, and
`assets/tmforum/PROVENANCE.md` records the commit and SHA-256 of each file.

TM Forum has not produced, reviewed or endorsed anything this project derives from those documents.

**TMF641 Service Ordering v5 is NOT here, and that is a finding rather than an omission.** Its origin
could not be established: the only Service Ordering repository in the Apache-2.0 organisation holds no
v5 document. `scripts/_corpora.py` still locates it at runtime for anyone who has a copy, and
`assets/tmforum/PROVENANCE.md` states what was searched.

This section said "**Not redistributed** ... obtain them from TM Forum directly" until 2026-09-25, which
was true when written and false the moment the two Apache-2.0 documents were vendored. A licence
statement that has quietly stopped matching the tree is worse than none.

